{"name":"Faded Grey","hex":"#eae8e4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"faded","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["That has lost some of its former vividness and colour.","That has lost some of its former strength or vigour."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of fade"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/faded"},{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Faded (Alan Walker song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Faded\" is a song by Norwegian DJ and record producer Alan Walker with vocals by Norwegian singer-songwriter Iselin Solheim. A rework of Walker's earlier song \"Fade\", the song was written by Walker, Jesper Borgen, Mood Melodies, and Gunnar Greve and produced by the former three. It was released as a single by MER on 3 December 2015, for digital download and streaming."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/da/Alan_Walker_-_Faded.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Faded_(Alan_Walker_song)"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg/330px-Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Alan_Walker_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Alan_Walker_%28cr